 ## Overview
-Bundle parallelisation distributes the processing of ray bundles across multiple processing elements to accelerate coherent grid traversal. It solves the performance bottleneck of serial ray integration by exploiting the spatial coherence of rays within a bundle. Unlike slice parallelisation, which requires complex index tables to map bundles to slices, bundle parallelisation processes bundles directly, though it may result in redundant block fetches from neighbouring bundles [S1, unofficial].
+Bundle parallelisation is a parallelization scheme for coherent grid traversal where bundles of rays are processed in parallel [S1, unofficial]. It distributes the processing of ray bundles across multiple processing elements to accelerate volume rendering [S3]. Unlike slice parallelisation, which requires complex index tables to map bundles to slices, bundle parallelisation processes bundles directly, though it may result in redundant block fetches from neighbouring bundles [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
